              "text": "しやくしょ (shiyakusho) is Sino-Japanese (kango): three Chinese characters read with their on'yomi, readings borrowed from Chinese. They are shi, \"market, city\" (Middle Chinese dzyiX), yaku, \"duty, office\" (ywek) and sho, \"place\" (srjoX) (KANJIDIC2; Middle Chinese in Baxter's transcription)."
